<div class="notice">
  <p><strong>How an amendment passes.</strong> Each amendment is a yes-or-no question listed directly after the governor's race. It passes only if both are true:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>it gets more "yes" votes than "no" votes, <em>and</em></li>
    <li>its "yes" votes are more than half of all votes cast in the governor's race.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="small muted" style="margin:0">
    Because of the second rule, leaving an amendment question blank works against it the same way a "no" vote does.
    Source: <a href="https://sos.tn.gov/elections/announcements/2026-proposed-constitutional-amendments">Tennessee Secretary of State</a>.
    <a href={url('method')}>More on how this guide works</a>.
  </p>
</div>
